00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,572
Day 60: codegraph, a local call graph index that lets a coding

2
00:00:04,572 --> 00:00:08,850
agent query code in one shot instead of repeating grep and

3
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:09,218
read.

4
00:00:09,668 --> 00:00:12,622
Codegraph scans a repo, builds a call graph,

5
00:00:12,622 --> 00:00:16,717
and lets an agent ask one query instead of repeating grep and

6
00:00:16,717 --> 00:00:17,052
read.

7
00:00:17,502 --> 00:00:21,543
We ran this on our own 159 file repo.

8
00:00:21,543 --> 00:00:26,785
Init parsed every file and wrote 2,162 nodes and

9
00:00:26,785 --> 00:00:31,481
4,700 edges to local SQLite in 2.6 seconds.

10
00:00:31,931 --> 00:00:34,687
Callers traced correctly across files,

11
00:00:34,687 --> 00:00:38,096
even through a renamed JavaScript export alias,

12
00:00:38,096 --> 00:00:40,127
something grep alone misses.

13
00:00:40,577 --> 00:00:44,101
But a query only matches the original declared name,

14
00:00:44,101 --> 00:00:47,218
and it only follows call edges, never meaning.

15
00:00:47,668 --> 00:00:50,853
We wrote two functions with identical logic but

16
00:00:50,853 --> 00:00:51,937
no shared calls.

17
00:00:51,937 --> 00:00:55,597
Impact and callers found zero connection between them,

18
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:57,223
confirming a real limit:

19
00:00:57,223 --> 00:01:00,544
duplicate logic is invisible without a call edge.

